     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · BS Personal Finance · 2026-10-14 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Bank of Baroda shares fall 3% amid $15 billion lawsuit report</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Bank of Baroda (BoB) shares dipped 3.4 percent on Wednesday following reports that B R Shetty, founder of the NMC Healthcare group, filed a $15 billion lawsuit against the bank in the Bombay High Court. The suit alleges that BoB facilitated fund diversion, ignored anti-money laundering alerts, and concealed liabilities.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-14/bank-of-baroda-shares-fall-3-amid-15-billion-lawsuit-report.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In an exchange filing, the bank stated it has not been served with the suit and cannot comment on untested allegations. Despite the decline, brokerages maintain a positive outlook for the bank, with analysts expecting double-digit profit-after-tax growth in the second quarter driven by stake sale gains and lower provisions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief correctly identifies the stock impact, the nature of the lawsuit, the bank's denial, and the analyst outlooks.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/bank-of-baroda-down-3-top-loser-in-psu-banks-why-is-the-stock-falling-126101400313_1.html" rel="noopener">BS Personal Finance</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
