       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-14 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Deezer Announces New Toggle to Filter Out AI-Generated Music by Year's End</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Streaming platform Deezer is developing a new user toggle designed to completely filter out AI-generated music from search results and feeds. The feature is scheduled for rollout before the end of the year in response to clear user demand for focusing exclusively on human creators. Deezer CEO Alexis Lanternier noted that the explosive growth of AI tracks catalyzed the feature, citing data showing AI content surpassed 50% of daily uploads by July. Competitors have implemented varying policies, ranging from Bandcamp completely banning AI tracks to Spotify solely applying prominence tags.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-14/deezer-announces-new-toggle-to-filter-out-ai-generated-music.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate, highly dense summary capturing all concrete details and stats from the source.</p>
