       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-14 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>ECI Extends SIR Deadline in Andhra Pradesh with Final Electoral Rolls Due October 30</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Election Commission of India has revised the Special Intensive Revision schedule for electoral rolls in Andhra Pradesh. The deadline for the notice phase and the disposal of claims and objections has been extended to October 22, 2026. Following this adjustment, the final electoral roll will be published on October 30, 2026. The revision uses July 1, 2026, as the qualifying date, and authorities have been directed to ensure wide publicity across all available media alongside written notifications to political parties.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-14/eci-extends-sir-deadline-in-andhra-pradesh-with-final-electo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Every concrete figure and date matches the source precisely.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
