     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-14 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kochi Synagogue Arson: NIA, Kerala ATS Probe Terror Links, $2,000 Payment</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Kochi</span> <span>#Synagogue</span> <span>#Arson</span> <span>#NIA</span></div>
       <p>The investigation into an alleged arson attempt outside a historic Kochi synagogue has expanded, with the National Investigation Agency (NIA) and Kerala Anti-Terrorism Squad (ATS) now examining suspected terror links, potential international connections, and financial transactions. Police are probing whether the accused, Ebin Paul, acted alone or as part of a larger network, according to investigators.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-14/kochi-synagogue-arson-nia-kerala-ats-probe-terror-links-2000.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The incident reportedly occurred around 2:30 am when Paul allegedly arrived with a can of petrol, poured it on horticulture nursery banners and flex boards run by the synagogue trust, and attempted to set them on fire. He was subsequently arrested. Investigators are also examining his suspected involvement in a similar arson incident in Muvattupuzha, though a connection is yet to be established.</p><p>Sources indicate investigators are scrutinizing Paul's activity in Telegram groups, where he is suspected of seeking tasks or instructions. Inputs suggest he may have received approximately $2,000 in connection with the synagogue incident. Police are verifying these claims, including the money transfer, facilitators, and the transaction's link to the arson attempt, as they seek to establish motive and identify associates.</p><p>Paul's mobile phone and its contents are under scrutiny, with preliminary inputs raising questions about contacts. A forensic examination is anticipated to authenticate communications and identify potential links to the incident. The probe also focuses on a suspected international angle, examining whether individuals or groups outside India directed, financed, or facilitated the alleged act, though these links remain under verification.</p><p>What to watch: Verification of financial records and digital forensics to establish the full scope of the incident.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is comprehensive and accurately reflects all details provided in the source text, including the specific investigative leads and the nature of the suspect's alleged actions.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/kochi-synagogue-fire-nia-kerala-ats-examine-suspected-terror-links-2000-payment-under-probe-ws-lr-10380986.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/kochi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kochi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
