     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-10-14 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Over 1,000 MBBS Seats Delayed, Out of Reach for Top Scorers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#MBBS</span> <span>#Medical Education</span> <span>#Government Colleges</span> <span>#Counselling</span></div>
       <p>More than 1,000 MBBS seats in government colleges are reportedly becoming available too late in the admissions process, disadvantaging higher-scoring students. This situation prevents these students from securing government seats during regular counselling rounds, according to experts.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-14/over-1000-mbbs-seats-delayed-out-of-reach-for-top-scorers.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>By the time these government seats become accessible in the &quot;stray round,&quot; many high-achieving students have already enrolled in private medical institutions. These private colleges typically charge around ₹30 lakh a year, representing a significant financial commitment.</p><p>Experts highlight that once students are enrolled in these costly private institutions, they are unable to upgrade to the more affordable government seats that become available later. This timing issue effectively keeps government-subsidized medical education out of reach for some of the most meritorious candidates.</p><p>What to watch: Potential changes in counselling timelines to ensure equitable access to government medical seats.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the core issue of the counselling timeline and the financial burden mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/education/over-1000-mbbs-seats-in-govt-colleges-open-up-too-late-for-higher-scorers/134937379" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-14/over-1000-mbbs-seats-delayed-out-of-reach-for-top-scorers" data-title="Over 1,000 MBBS Seats Delayed, Out of Reach for Top Scorers"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
         <a class="sh-tg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M14.4 1.6 1.6 7l3.6 1.2L6 13l2.2-3.1 3.4 2.4 2.8-10.7z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Telegram</a> ·
         <a class="sh-x" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.6 2.6l10.8 10.8M13.4 2.6 2.6 13.4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>X</a> ·
