       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-14 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Owaisi advises youth to marry before declaring love</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>AIMIM chief Asaduddin Owaisi has advised young men to marry before telling a woman &quot;I love you,&quot; stating that marriage completes half of one's faith. Addressing a gathering, he dismissed the notion of needing to &quot;get settled&quot; financially before marriage, suggesting that life will fall into place afterward.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-14/owaisi-advises-youth-to-marry-before-declaring-love.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Owaisi has frequently expressed views on social issues, including his opposition to the proposed Uniform Civil Code, which he argues could erode India's religious diversity. He also maintains that marriage should be strictly between a man and a woman, and that legal recognition of same-sex marriage should be decided by Parliament rather than the judiciary.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes Owaisi's statements and his broader political stances using the provided source text.</p>
