     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-14 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rajinikanth's 'Jailer 2' Generates Buzz with Rs 50 Crore Advance Bookings Ahead of October 15 Release</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Jailer 2</span> <span>#Rajinikanth</span> <span>#Nelson Dilipkumar</span> <span>#Bjorn</span></div>
       <p>Anticipation for Rajinikanth’s 'Jailer 2', directed by Nelson Dilipkumar, is reaching a fever pitch just hours before its release. Strong advance bookings and cast updates have significantly heightened expectations for the sequel’s opening-day performance on October 15. Fans are eagerly awaiting what director Nelson Dilipkumar has planned for the film.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-14/rajinikanths-jailer-2-generates-buzz-with-rs-50-crore-advanc.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Actor Bjorn has further fueled curiosity with a social media post, hinting at a &quot;Silent Sambavam&quot; (silent event) in the film. Bjorn wrote, &quot;I know something you don’t! Silent sambavam irukku. October 15th, you’ll know too!&quot; He added, &quot;Super stoked to be a part of JAILER 2! Can’t wait for you guys to experience this one on the big screen. Total fun only!&quot; These comments have led to speculation about a surprise sequence or a memorable moment, though Bjorn did not reveal any specific details.</p><p>According to Sacnilk, 'Jailer 2' has reportedly surpassed Rs 50 crore in worldwide advance bookings, setting the stage for a strong opening. Fans are expressing hopes for the film to join the Rs 100 crore worldwide opening-day club, with some even discussing its potential to reach the Rs 1,000 crore mark. However, the film's ultimate box office performance will depend on immediate audience reactions, critical reviews, and its ability to sustain momentum post-release.</p><p>The film features a prominent cast alongside Rajinikanth, including Ramya Krishnan, Yogi Babu, Mohanlal, Shivarajkumar, Suraj Venjaramoodu, SJ Suryah, Vidya Balan, and Vijay Sethupathi. The music for the sequel has been composed by Anirudh Ravichander, adding another layer of excitement for its October 15 theatrical release. Whether Bjorn's teased &quot;silent sambavam&quot; becomes a standout moment will be revealed to audiences soon.</p><p>What to watch: Opening day box office figures and early audience and critical reviews.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately covers the box office expectations, cast, and social media buzz mentioned in the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/tamil/movies/news/jailer-2-rajinikanth-starrer-is-a-silent-sambavam-says-bjorn-as-nelsons-film-surpasses-rs-50-crore-in-advance-bookings/articleshow/134931988.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
