     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · BBC Business · 2026-10-14 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Wayfair, Appliances Direct and Gold's Gym Fined £6m for Misleading Tactics</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Competition and Markets Authority has fined Wayfair £4.8m, Appliances Direct £1.2m, and Gold's Gym £48,000 for using illegal, misleading sales tactics. Wayfair and Appliances Direct were penalized for deceptive time-limited offers, while Gold's Gym failed to disclose total membership costs. All three firms admitted to breaking the law and settled early, which reduced their fines by 40%.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-14/wayfair-appliances-direct-and-golds-gym-fined-6m-for-mislead.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Appliances Direct and Gold's Gym must pay a combined £440,000 in refunds to thousands of affected customers. Appliances Direct is ordered to issue payments by 11 March, with Gold's Gym following by 29 March. Affected customers do not need to take action as the companies will initiate contact.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the fines and refund details, though it misses the specific detail that companies claimed the fines were disproportionate.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx298e5rr3po?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Business</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
